        case='''A fictitious local research team wants to understand how adults describe the transition into retirement. An authorised community organisation uses its membership list to send study invitations to randomly selected adults who recently retired. Researchers do not receive the contact list. Those who consent complete a postal questionnaire at home, with a separate telephone-completion option. Several items ask whether respondents feel able to organise their own daily activities; an open question invites them to explain what a satisfying day now means. Researchers test the wording with a small group before the main survey and offer both completion formats consistently. Some invited adults do not respond. The organisation includes members who joined organised activities, but not all retired residents. A researcher proposes that this random invitation procedure represents the whole local retired population and that respondents' descriptions of their earlier working lives will show how their independence has changed.''',
