        case='''A fictitious researcher investigates the relationship between participation in neighbourhood activities and adults' sense of belonging. Randomly selected members of several public-library mailing lists receive an invitation. Consenting adults complete a short belonging questionnaire and permit the researcher to ask how often they attended local activities during the previous month. No one is asked to join or avoid an activity. The questionnaire explains that there are no preferred answers and that library services will not be affected by participation. The researcher also asks about length of residence and availability of free time because these might be relevant to both activity attendance and belonging. The contact information is stored separately and deleted after participants have had an agreed opportunity to withdraw. A local newsletter editor wants to report that attending more activities creates a stronger sense of belonging. The researcher plans to explain what this correlational design could and could not justify.''',
